# Secrets defined here are available for reference under registry/password, env/secret, builder/secrets,
# and accessories/*/env/secret in config/deploy.yml. All secrets should be pulled from either
# password manager, ENV, or a file. DO NOT ENTER RAW CREDENTIALS HERE! This file needs to be safe for git.
# Explains the purpose of this file: it's a template that Kamal reads to resolve secret placeholders.
# It warns you to never paste real passwords directly, since this file is committed to version control.

# Example of extracting secrets from 1password (or another compatible pw manager)
# Shows how to fetch secrets from 1Password at deploy time using the Kamal CLI.
# SECRETS=$(kamal secrets fetch --adapter 1password --account your-account --from Vault/Item KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD RAILS_MASTER_KEY)
# This line would pull multiple secrets from your 1Password vault in one command.
# KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD=$(kamal secrets extract KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD ${SECRETS})
# Extracts just the registry password from the fetched secrets string.
# RAILS_MASTER_KEY=$(kamal secrets extract RAILS_MASTER_KEY ${SECRETS})
# Extracts just the Rails master key from the same fetched secrets string.

# Example of extracting secrets from Rails credentials
# Shows an alternative method: reading secrets from Rails' encrypted credentials store.
# KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD=$(rails credentials:fetch kamal.registry_password)
# Uses a Rails command to decrypt and retrieve the registry password from config/credentials.yml.enc.

# Use a GITHUB_TOKEN if private repositories are needed for the image
# Explains when you'd need a GitHub token (pulling from private repos during Docker build).
# GITHUB_TOKEN=$(gh config get -h github.com oauth_token)
# Reads the OAuth token from your local GitHub CLI (gh) configuration.

# Grab the registry password from ENV
# Shows the simplest approach: reading a secret directly from an environment variable.
# KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD=$KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD
# This line reads the KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD env var that you exported in your shell.

# Improve security by using a password manager. Never check config/master.key into git!
# Reminds you to use a password manager and keep the Rails master key out of version control.
RAILS_MASTER_KEY=$(cat config/master.key)
# Reads the Rails master key from the local file config/master.key.
# This key is used to decrypt Rails credentials and must stay secret in production.
